    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "A historic deluge, one of the heaviest rainy seasons in three decades, exposed the state's failure as reservoirs filled beyond capacity and infrastructure overwhelmed. The predictable consequence of climate neglect turned into a landscape of abandonment when surging flows submerged communities and livelihoods across the Syrian regions. The regime's clean-up crew deployed evacuation operations only after critical infrastructure failed, a token response to a systemic crisis. This is the ultimate price of institutional neglect, paid by the youngest victims.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "An external actor dictating terms became Syria's only lifeline, trading sovereignty for water as the upstream power agreed to a diplomatic concession on water flow. This move came after the failed defenses betraying public trust left submerged communities and livelihoods in its wake. The face of a failed state surveyed the damage his system caused, a performative concern from the top after a collapse emblematic of state decay. The abandoned generation was left to drown.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
        "fragments": [
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "how-4",
          "how-5",
